apeiron.machine.infinite_energy.desc=Debits the GT wireless network directly without a local energy cache\nVoltage and amperage projections use Integer.MAX_VALUE\nDefault parallel cap 2147483647; set 0 manually to remove the cap\nParallel and running voltage accept scientific notation\nNative machine overclock rules apply; raising voltage may increase total energy use\nWhole-batch energy and output capacity are checked before starting; low balance pauses\nParallel, EU/t, output and pending counts use exact big integers
apeiron.machine.ultimate_energy.desc=Debits the recipe base total energy directly from the GT wireless network\nDefault parallel cap 2147483647; set 0 manually to remove the cap\nDefault 128 ticks (6.4 seconds), minimum 1 tick\nChanging completion time does not change total energy\nWhole-batch energy, ingredients and output capacity are checked before starting
apeiron.machine.energy.parallel_hint=Accepts 1E20 and 1e20; default 2147483647, manually set 0 for no fixed cap
